{
  "name": "Listen Route Respond (Core) – DEMO",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1 – Listen\n**Webhook** waits for a browser or app to call its URL.\nTest it (click *Listen for test event* first):\n`…/webhook-test/lab3-products?tier=high&limit=3`\n\nRead the query values with `{{ $json.query.tier }}`.\n**webhook-test** works only while listening; **/webhook/** works only when the workflow is **Active**.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "243626ea-9bee-44ff-b847-576fa9ddd854",
      "name": "Note – Listen",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -528,
        -240
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2 – Route\n**If** checks that `tier` was sent.\n**Switch** sends the products down one of 3 paths (high / medium / low) – each with its own **Filter** price range.\nAnything else goes to the **invalid** output.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 900,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "e5511efa-43e1-4b55-87d9-9d364ceb76a4",
      "name": "Note – Route",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        176,
        -240
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3 – Respond\n**Respond to Webhook** sends your own JSON back to the caller (200).\nBad requests get **Respond to Webhook1** (400), then **Stop and Error** marks the run as failed so you see it in *Executions*.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nby Naji El Kotob + AI",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 800,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "f9505cc3-a654-4ef8-9675-4a69632205b8",
      "name": "Note – Respond",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1136,
        -240
      ]
    },
